" data-formats="free-response multiple-choice" id="511937"><span class="os-number">7</span>
<span class="os-divider">. </span>

<div class="os-problem-container">
  
  
  <div data-type="question-stem">What is inertia?</div>
  <ol data-type="question-answers" type="a">
            <li data-type="question-answer" data-correctness="">
                <div data-type="answer-content">Inertia is an object’s tendency to maintain its mass.</div>
                
            </li>
            <li data-type="question-answer" data-correctness="">
                <div data-type="answer-content">Inertia is an object’s tendency to remain at rest.</div>
                
            </li>
            <li data-type="question-answer" data-correctness="">
                <div data-type="answer-content">Inertia is an object’s tendency to remain in motion</div>
                
            </li>
            <li data-type="question-answer" data-correctness="">
                <div data-type="answer-content">Inertia is an object’s tendency to remain at rest or, if moving, to remain in motion.</div>
                
            </li>
            </ol>
</div>

        
        
        </div>
    </div><div data-type="exercise" id="fs-idp86925600" class="os-exercise"><header></header><section><div data-type="problem" id="fs-idp30536672">
<span class="os-number">8</span><span class="os-divider">. </span>
<div class="os-problem-container">
<!--<para id="fs-idm16321040"><link class="os-embed" url="#ost/api/ex/k12phys-ch04-ex021"/></para>-->

<p id="fs-id1164567999263">What is mass? What does it depend on?</p>
<ol id="fs-id1164567620406" type="a">
<li>Mass is the weight of an object, and it depends on the gravitational force acting on the object.</li>
<li>Mass is the weight of an object, and it depends on the number and types of atoms in the object.</li>
<li>Mass is the quantity of matter contained in an object, and it depends on the gravitational force acting on the object.</li>
<li>Mass is the quantity of matter contained in an object, and it depends on the number and types of atoms in the object.</li>
</ol>
</div>
</div></section></div>
</section>














